WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.470
The Humber: the largest estuary
on Britain's east coast.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.430
It is a muddy, macro-tidal
estuary, fed by the Ouse,

3
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.430
the Trent and other rivers.

4
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.510
But some of its mud
comes from up the coast:

5
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.110
Holderness, where cliffs of
boulder clay are eroding.

6
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.490
So how does a crumbling cliff become mud,

7
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.510
and then new land?

8
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.170
Do waves pile it up?

9
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.670
Do plants make it?

10
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.330
In this mission, you'll explore the
physical factors that shape this coast:

11
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.610
geology, sea level and sediment supply.

12
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:34.950
Then you'll trace how
the landscape changes,

13
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.290
from a single tide to thousands of years.

14
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.840
Your mission: explain how mud from
crumbling cliffs becomes land.
